    <h4>2. Competent supervisory authority</h4>
    <p>As determined by applying Clause 13 of the EU SCCs. For Processing subject to the DPDP Act, the Data Protection Board of India.</p>
    <h4>3. Processing information</h4>
    <div class="lg-table-wrap">
      <table class="lg-table lg-table--kv">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Categories of data subjects</th><td><p>End Users who interact with the Customer's applications, websites or agents through the Services.</p><p>The Customer's authorised users of the console and APIs.</p></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Categories of personal data</th><td>
            <p>Processed automatically by the Services:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>End User voice audio, carried in real time;</li>
              <li>transcripts of what End Users say and of the agent's replies;</li>
              <li>session metadata, such as session identifiers, timestamps, duration, IP address, device and browser details, and connection quality;</li>
              <li>session events, including events from the Customer's application that the Customer chooses to send;</li>
              <li>names and email addresses of the Customer's authorised users.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Processed only where and to the extent the Customer enables or provides it:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>recordings of audio, and of camera or screen video sent by the Customer's application;</li>
              <li>context the Customer passes when starting a session (Voqalize recommends identifiers rather than personal data);</li>
              <li>personal data contained in the instructions, knowledge or tool results the Customer configures for Plug &amp; Play.</li>
            </ul>
          </td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Sensitive data</th><td>None intended. End Users may disclose sensitive information in conversation; it is protected with the measures in section 4. Voice Data is not used for biometric identification (section 6.3).</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Frequency of transfer</th><td>Continuous, for the duration of each session.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Nature of processing</th><td>Receiving and transmitting real-time audio and video; speech to text; text to speech; turn-taking and interruption handling; generating the on-screen character's movement from the agent's speech; forwarding text and events to the Customer's brain and tools; in Plug &amp; Play, generating replies with a language model; recording and storing sessions where enabled; logging, monitoring and support. The purpose is to perform the Services described in the Agreement and order forms.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Retention</th><td>Stored session data (the session record, events, transcripts, logs and recordings) is retained for 30 days, unless the Agreement or order form sets another period, and is then deleted. Account data of authorised users is retained while the account is open and for 90 days after.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Sub-processor transfers</th><td>As listed in Annex 2, for the subject matter, nature and duration described there and in the Agreement.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h4>Business Purposes for California consumers</h4>
    <p>For Processing involving California consumers, Voqalize Processes Personal Data for these Business Purposes:</p>
    <ul class="lg-checks">
      <li class="is-on">Helping to ensure security and integrity, to the extent the use of the consumer's personal information is reasonably necessary and proportionate for these purposes.</li>
      <li class="is-on">Debugging to identify and repair errors that impair existing intended functionality.</li>
      <li class="is-on">Performing services on behalf of the business, including maintaining or servicing accounts, providing customer service, processing or fulfilling orders and transactions, verifying customer information, processing payments, providing analytic services, providing storage, or providing similar services on behalf of the business.</li>
      <li class="is-on">Undertaking activities to verify or maintain the quality or safety of a service that is owned or controlled by the business.</li>
      <li class="is-on">Retaining and employing another service provider or contractor as a subcontractor, where the subcontractor meets the requirements for a service provider or contractor under the CCPA.</li>
      <li class="is-on">Preventing, detecting or investigating data security incidents, or protecting against malicious, deceptive, fraudulent or illegal activity.</li>
      <li>Undertaking internal research for technological development and demonstration. Not selected (see section 6.4).</li>
      <li>Building or improving the quality of the services provided to the business. Not selected (see section 6.4).</li>
      <li>Short-term, transient use, or advertising and marketing services.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lg-sec" id="annex-1-security" aria-labelledby="annex-1-security-h">
  <h3 class="lg-sec__h" id="annex-1-security-h"><span class="lg-sec__n">A1.4</span> Technical and organisational security measures<a class="lg-anchor" href="#annex-1-security" aria-label="Link to Annex 1, section 4">#</a></h3>
  <p class="lg-short"><b>In short.</b> The security measures we use to protect your data.</p>
  <div class="lg-body">
    <p>The technical and organisational measures Voqalize implements as the processor and data importer to ensure an appropriate level of security, taking into account the nature, scope, context and purpose of the Processing and the risks to the rights and freedoms of natural persons.</p>
    <h4>Security management</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Organisation.</b> Voqalize designates qualified security personnel responsible for developing, implementing and maintaining its information security program.</li>
      <li><b>Policies.</b> Management reviews and supports all security policies to protect the security, availability, integrity and confidentiality of Customer Personal Data. Policies are reviewed at least once a year.</li>
      <li><b>Assessments.</b> Voqalize engages a reputable independent third party to perform risk assessments of systems containing Customer Personal Data at least once a year.</li>
      <li><b>Risk treatment.</b> Voqalize maintains a risk treatment program that includes vulnerability management and patch management, and engages an independent third party to perform a vulnerability assessment and penetration test (VAPT) at least once a year.</li>
      <li><b>Vendor management.</b> Voqalize assesses Sub-processors before engaging them and reviews them periodically.</li>
      <li><b>Incident management.</b> Voqalize reviews security incidents, determines root cause and takes corrective action.</li>
      <li><b>Standards.</b> ISO/IEC 27001:2022 certified; SOC 2 compliant; GDPR and DPDP Act compliant.</li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Personnel security</h4>
    <p>Voqalize personnel must act in line with the company's guidelines on confidentiality, business ethics, appropriate use and professional standards. Voqalize conducts reasonably appropriate background checks on employees who will have access to Customer Personal Data, to the extent legally permitted and in line with local labour law and practice. Personnel sign a confidentiality agreement when hired, acknowledge Voqalize's confidentiality, privacy and security policies, and receive privacy and security training. Personnel do not Process Customer Personal Data without authorisation.</p>
    <h4>Access controls</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Access management.</b> Access to Customer Personal Data and to the systems that store or transmit it is requested, approved and provisioned through a formal process, limited to authorised people with a need for access, and reviewed periodically.</li>
      <li><b>Least privilege.</b> Systems allow people to access only the data they are authorised to access, based on least privilege and need to know. Unique user IDs, strong authentication and monitored access lists are required. Access to systems is logged to create an audit trail.</li>
      <li><b>Authentication.</b> Console users sign in through a single sign-on provider. API access requires secret keys held on the Customer's server; client code uses publishable keys restricted to allowed origins. Keys can be revoked at any time.</li>
      <li><b>Tenant isolation.</b> Each Customer's data is logically separated, and every request is authorised against the Customer it names before any data is read.</li>
      <li><b>Audit trail.</b> Sign-ins, key creation and revocation, and administrative actions are logged and retained for 400 days.</li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Infrastructure and network security</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Infrastructure.</b> All of the Services, including the control plane, database, storage, real-time voice runtime and speech models, run on Google Cloud Platform in the Mumbai region (asia-south1), India.</li>
      <li><b>Resiliency and recovery.</b> Data is replicated to protect against accidental destruction or loss, and backup restoration and disaster recovery are tested regularly.</li>
      <li><b>Hardening and code review.</b> Servers are configured and hardened for the Services. Code changes go through review before release.</li>
      <li><b>Logging and monitoring.</b> Systems log security-relevant events to support audits and to detect actual and attempted intrusions.</li>
      <li><b>Vulnerability management.</b> Regular vulnerability scans cover production infrastructure. Critical, high and medium vulnerabilities are remediated on a risk basis as soon as commercially possible.</li>
      <li><b>Network protection.</b> Production systems sit behind firewalls that restrict inbound traffic to the services that need it.</li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Encryption, storage and deletion</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><b>In transit.</b> Real-time audio and video are encrypted with DTLS-SRTP. All other traffic uses TLS.</li>
      <li><b>At rest.</b> Stored Customer Personal Data, including recordings, is encrypted at rest.</li>
      <li><b>Recordings.</b> Recordings are retrieved only through signed links that expire within 15 minutes.</li>
      <li><b>Deletion.</b> Stored session data is deleted automatically at the end of its retention period by storage lifecycle rules, and on request. Retired storage media are disposed of securely by the infrastructure provider.</li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Incident response</h4>
    <p>Voqalize maintains incident management policies and procedures, including escalation procedures. Security personnel respond promptly to suspected or known incidents, mitigate harmful effects, and document incidents and their outcomes.</p>
  </div>
</section>

